        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "According to the data, is having a driver’s licence dependent on gender?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "No. Having a licence and gender are independent in the survey data.",
          "worked": "The overall licence rate is $P(\\text{licence})=\\frac{75}{100}=\\frac34$. From part (a), the licence rate is also $\\frac34$ within each gender. Knowing the student's gender leaves the probability of having a licence unchanged, so licence status and gender are independent in the survey data.",
